        The deployment of generative artificial intelligence has historically been constrained to cloud-hosted clusters of high-bandwidth memory GPUs (NVIDIA H100s and A100s). For client-side web applications, attempting to run standard 7-billion parameter models (such as Llama-3-8B or Mistral-7B) in browser tabs causes immediate tab crashes, as browser memory allocators routinely kill any JavaScript process demanding more than 2GB to 4GB of contiguous heap.
      </p>
